      "response": {
        "answer": "The Pragati Scholarship Schemes (for technical degree and diploma students) and the AICTE Saksham Scholarship Scheme (for specially-abled students pursuing a degree) each provide an annual amount of \u20b950,000. All three schemes share the application method of applying online through the National Scholarship Portal. Regarding eligibility, Pragati schemes are restricted to female students studying in AICTE-approved institutions with a family income up to \u20b98,00,000 per annum. Similarly, the Saksham scheme requires enrollment in an AICTE-approved institution with a family income not exceeding \u20b98 lakh per annum, but specifically requires students to be specially-abled with a disability of at least 40%.",
